'' A label after EXIT SUB or RETURN. See the source for what was dropped and why it
'' matters.
''
'' THE FIX IS IN THE STATEMENT DISPATCH, not at the terminator. Opening an "after" block
'' at every RETURN was tried and reverted -- lowerinit.bas records that it left one
'' unreachable block, and one unreachable 'ret', per return in the corpus, 1,488 of them.
'' Nothing needs a block there unless a label follows, and a label opens its own.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/label-after-exit.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' BOTH labels get a block, and both bodies are in it.
'' EXPECT-OUT: lbl.tail4:
'' EXPECT-OUT: lbl.tail24:
'' GOLDEN: expected/label-after-exit.out
